rotails","id":10767978,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzY3OTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10767978?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails","html_url":"https://github.com/retrotails","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-13T03:33:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-13T03:33:00Z","body":"I have written a better attempt than the previous hack. this patch adds `frustum_offset` to CameraData, which is read into RenderSceneDataRD as `cam_frustum_offset`, and finally makes it's way to GI::process_gi.\n\nhttps://github.com/retrotails/godot/commit/c03d7bfffa02eb367d0429f076462e2e26e5f8f5\n(note that this patch fixes Voxel GI and SDFGI, unlike the previous hack it does not attempt to fix the screen space effects)\n\nI still don't exactly understand what the issue is. it looks like process_gi is using a projection matrix that already had the frustum offset applied by set_frustum(); maybe the GI needs the projection matrix *without* the projection offset, and my code is doing the inverse?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3066481918/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_a